questions.question_text:
$7$ points are marked on the circumference of a circle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) circle (2.2);
\fill (90:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above] {$P_1$};
\fill (38.57:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$P_2$};
\fill (-12.86:2.2) circle (2pt) node[right] {$P_3$};
\fill (-64.29:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$P_4$};
\fill (-115.71:2.2) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$P_5$};
\fill (-167.14:2.2) circle (2pt) node[left] {$P_6$};
\fill (141.43:2.2) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$P_7$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
How many triangles can be formed using these points as vertices?
